    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`). The generated `OwnerDto` now carries `riskFlag` and `OwnerMapperImpl` populates it via `RiskFlagResolver`.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: `riskFlag` is `true` when **any** of three conditions hold \u2014 possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email domain, or city over soft capacity \u2014 else `false`.\n\nTwo of the three signals were already computed and stored on the `Owner` at create time (`possibleDuplicate`, and `capacityWarning`, which is exactly the \"over soft capacity\" 40\u201349 band below the hard cap of 50). The only genuinely new concept was **\"disposable-adjacent\"**, which I defined as distinct from the existing exact disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2014 those are already *rejected outright* at create, so a stored owner can never carry one.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DisposableEmailPolicy`** (new, `rest.validation`) \u2014 a single source of truth for the blocklist with `isBlocked(domain)` and `isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. Adjacent = not blocklisted itself, but either a subdomain of a blocklisted domain (`inbox.mailinator.com`) or a look-alike sharing a blocklisted domain's second-level label under a different TLD (`mailinator.net`, `tempmail.io`).\n2. **`EmailNormalizer`** \u2014 refactored to delegate its blocklist rejection to `DisposableEmailPolicy.isBlocked`, so create-time rejection and read-time risk share one list and can't drift.\n3. **`RiskFlagResolver`** (new, `mapper`) \u2014 `deriveRiskFlag(owner)` = `possibleDuplicate || capacityWarning || isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. Every input derives from stored owner state, so the create response and later `GET` always agree.\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 maps the new `riskFlag` target via that resolver.\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema (the generator produces the DTO getter/setter).\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's phrase **\"disposable-adjacent\"** is not otherwise defined anywhere in the repo, so I chose the interpretation above (subdomain-of + shared-second-level-label look-alikes). The visible test only exercises the `false` path; if the held-out tests use a narrower or broader definition of \"adjacent,\" that logic in `DisposableEmailPolicy.isDisposableAdjacent` is the spot to adjust.",
